Z||000003||Robert||10-23-2000||09:10 PM||||Well-done Mike!!!<P>How did you handle the paint?  Did you just paint the new parts or the whole car?  I bet your neighbors think you traded in your “old” car for this “new” one.<P>Keep up the GOOD work.<P>Robert<P><P>------------------<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://canterburytrails.com/photo/T2.GIF"> ||||reg||10
Z||000004||mbramble||10-23-2000||09:31 PM||||Sushi, Sunroof wasn't too bad at all but you do need a donor car.  There are very good instructions here: <A HREF="http://www.cyberverse.com/~cyco/fieroparts/tips/sunroof.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.cyberverse.com/~cyco/fieroparts/tips/sunroof.htm</A> <P><BR>Robert, I painted the fascia and sunroof skin (the donor was silver) using cans of Dupli-Color touch up spray paint and cans of clearcoat.  I also sanded the clearcoat on the front hood and put new clearcoat there.  It was in pretty bad shape in several places.  Turned out pretty good though.  Will eventually have th whole car painted (or maybe even do it myself now that some of the mystery is out of the process).<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Tigger||10-23-2000||09:34 PM||||Looks cool man, nice work!<P>------------------<BR>T-T-F-N, Tah Tah For Now!<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tigger.gif">           <BR>  <A HREF="mailto:RacingStripes@hotmail.com">RacingStripes@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||14
